# close-completeness gate — enforcement sentinel (#1290)
#
# This committed marker governs whether the close-completeness gate
# (`deploy.sh --check-close-completeness`, i.e. Check 48's verdict) BLOCKS or merely
# REPORTS on an INCOMPLETE verdict. The probe reads this file directly, so the
# sentinel is load-bearing on its own; a thin CI workflow can additionally consume
# the probe's exit code once wired.
#
# The first non-comment, non-blank line is the mode token:
#   warn      → report only (exit-0); a finding is surfaced but does not block.
#   enforce   → block on an INCOMPLETE verdict (exit-1 propagates to any CI caller).
#
# Ships DORMANT (warn) during the calibration window, per the warn-mode-initial
# posture and the reflexive-pipeline-loop discipline (the introducing release
# v2.37 closes under the pre-merge runbook; the gate's row-cutover is anchored
# strictly AFTER this release's merge). Flip the token below to `enforce` after a
# >=3-day warn-log review with zero false positives — that single edit, plus
# setting CLOSE_COMPLETENESS_CHECK_CUTOFF to the first post-v2.37 release, arms
# the gate. No code change is needed to graduate.
#
# (Content-flagged rather than presence-flagged so the file can ship now — the
#  docs reference it — while the gate stays non-blocking; the version-freeness
#  sentinel is presence-flagged, this one is mode-token-flagged.)
warn
